---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
---
<Layout
  title="News & Events"
  description="Local-first news and events for Azizi Riviera residents — what's actually happening in the development, not another citywide press release."
>
  <section class="container hero">
    <p class="eyebrow">News & events</p>
    <h1>What's on, locally</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      Dubai has no shortage of citywide event coverage already. This page
      exists for the other kind: what's happening in Riviera itself and
      immediately around it — promenade openings, community meetups, and
      the kind of local news that a citywide outlet has no reason to cover.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="container">
    <h2>What counts as "local" here</h2>
    <p>
      New promenade tenants opening, community events organized by residents
      or building management, seasonal changes to the canal walkway, and
      anything specific to living in Riviera rather than Dubai generally.
      Citywide festivals and events get plenty of coverage elsewhere; this
      page deliberately doesn't duplicate that.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="container">
    <h2>Follow along</h2>
    <p>
      The fastest-moving version of this content lives on Instagram
      (<strong>@rivieradst</strong>) rather than here — this page is the
      durable, searchable record of what's been happening, while the
      Instagram account is where it happens first.
    </p>
  </section>
</Layout>

<style>
  .hero { padding-top: var(--space-5); }
  .lede { font-size: var(--step-1); color: var(--ink-muted); max-width: 65ch; }
</style>
